    <link-summary>Learn how you can forward %product% reports to %cloud% using Docker images, Qodana CLI, and all CI/CD software
        we currently provide integration solutions for.</link-summary>

    <p>This section explains how you can forward %instance% reports to %cloud% using this software:</p>

    <list>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-local-run">Docker and %product% CLI</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-azure">Azure Pipelines</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-bitbucket">Bitbucket Cloud</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-circleci">CircleCI</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-github-actions">GitHub Actions</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-gitlab-ci">GitLab CI/CD</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-jenkins">Jenkins</a></li>
        <li><a anchor="cloud-forward-reports-teamcity">TeamCity</a></li>
    </list>

    <note>To provide the correct work of the contributor counting functionality, add the IP address range
        54.76.32.8/32 to a list of allowed inbound connections on your side.
    </note>

    <chapter id="cloud-forward-reports-before-you-start" title="Before you start">
