    <chapter id="cloud-forward-reports-gitlab-ci" title="GitLab CI/CD">
        <procedure>
            <step>
                <p>Prepare your project as described in the <a href="gitlab.md" anchor="Before+you+start"/> section.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In the root folder of your GitLab-hosted project, create the <code>.gitlab-ci.yml</code> file and save this
                    configuration to that file:</p>
                <code-block lang="yaml">
                  include:
                      - component: %gitlab-version%
                        inputs:
                            args: --image &lt;image&gt;
                </code-block>
            </step>
        </procedure>

        <p>To learn more about %instance% integration with GitLab CI/CD, see the <a href="gitlab.md"/> section of this
        documentation.</p>

    </chapter>

    <chapter id="cloud-forward-reports-jenkins" title="Jenkins">

        <procedure>
            <step>
                <p>In the Jenkins UI, create the credentials with the <code>qodana-token</code> name as described in the
                    <a href="https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/using/using-credentials/#adding-new-global-credentials">Adding new global credentials</a>
                    section of the Jenkins documentation, and save the
                    <a href="cloud-projects.topic" anchor="cloud-manage-projects">project token</a> as the value for these credentials.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In the root directory of your project, create the <code>Jenkinsfile</code> file and save this configuration to that file:</p>
                <code-block lang="groovy">
                    pipeline {
                       environment {
                          QODANA_TOKEN=credentials('qodana-token')
                       }
                       agent {
                          docker {
                             args '''
                             -v "${WORKSPACE}":/data/project
                             --entrypoint=""
                             '''
                             image 'jetbrains/qodana-&lt;image&gt;'
                          }
                       }
                       stages {
                          stage('Qodana') {
                             steps {
                                sh '''qodana'''
                             }
                          }
                       }
                    }
                </code-block>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In the <code>image</code> section of this script, specify the %instance% <a href="deploy-qodana.md" anchor="Docker+images">Docker image</a> name.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>

        <p>To learn more about %instance% integration with Jenkins, see the <a href="jenkins.md"/> section of this
            documentation.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter id="cloud-forward-reports-teamcity" title="TeamCity">

        <procedure>
            <step>
                <p>In the TeamCity UI, open the build step that will run %instance%.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>In the <ui-path>Cloud Token</ui-path> field, insert the <a href="cloud-projects.topic" anchor="cloud-manage-projects">%cloud% token</a> value.</p>
                <img src="cloud-forward-reports-teamcity.png" width="706" alt="Configuring fields in TeamCity" border-effect="line"/>
            </step>
        </procedure>

        <p>To learn more about %instance% integration with TeamCity, see the <a href="teamcity.md"/> section of
            this documentation.</p>
        </chapter>
